      "math_academy_id": "e-8932",
      "problem": "Find the quotient and remainder of the following division problem:\n\n$$\n\\dfrac {5x^4- 2x^3 - 18x^2 + 11x - 13} {5x^2-2x+2}\n$$",
      "worked_solution": "Using the method of polynomial division, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{x}^{2}-4 \\\\  & 5{x}^{2}-2x+2\\,\\enclose{longdiv}{\\,\\,5{x}^{4}-2{x}^{3}-18{x}^{2}+11x-13\\,\\,} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{5{x}^{4}-2{x}^{3}+2{x}^{2}}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,-20{x}^{2}+11x-13 \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{-\\,20{x}^{2}+8x-8}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,3x-5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAs a result,\n\n- the quotient is $x^2-4,$ and\n\n- the remainder is $3x-5.$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n\\dfrac{5x^4-2x^3-18x^2+11x-13}{5x^2-2x+2}=x^2-4 + \\dfrac{3x-5}{5x^2-2x+2}.\n$$",
